IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgba-nouns`
IMPORT `sgba-seat`
IMPORT `sgba-tv-seat`

-- QUARANTINED (name starts sgba-tv-): worked cases for sgba-tv-seat.l4, the questions of the person who owns a television or a satellite dish.
-- Expected values are written from the text of the sections named in each comment (the Gazette's Revised Editions 2003 and 2012, S 549/2012, the consolidation in force 25 September 2024 to 4 November 2026; the TVRO System Regulations as deposited).
-- A case's outcome is what the cited provisions give on the facts stated; it is not a statement about any real person.
-- Argument order of "Am I contravening section 20(1)...": day; can receive a broadcasting service; can receive directly from a satellite; installs; imports/sells/holds for sale;
-- operates or has on own premises; services are received; under a licence; forces duty; Authority exemption; Ministerial order.

§ `1. Is my equipment broadcasting apparatus?`

-- Each pair of days, for each kind of equipment. The expected values are written from the First Schedule as the Gazette prints it: items 1 broadcast television receiver, 2 broadcast sound receiver and 3 TVRO system
-- in the Revised Editions 2003 and 2012; the TVRO system alone in S 549/2012 and in the 2024 consolidation. A television set is used for the visual and aural reception of a broadcasting service; a radio for aural reception.

-- P1: conduct 5 May 2005, read 1 June 2005: the Revised Edition 2003 is the text
#ASSERT `Is my equipment broadcasting apparatus, for that conduct, with the law read as at that day?` "television" (Date 5 5 2005) (Date 1 6 2005) EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `Is my equipment broadcasting apparatus, for that conduct, with the law read as at that day?` "FM radio" (Date 5 5 2005) (Date 1 6 2005) EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `Is my equipment broadcasting apparatus, for that conduct, with the law read as at that day?` "AM radio" (Date 5 5 2005) (Date 1 6 2005) EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `Is my equipment broadcasting apparatus, for that conduct, with the law read as at that day?` "satellite dish" (Date 5 5 2005) (Date 1 6 2005) EQUALS "Yes."
