§ `3. May I be granted a licence?`

-- reg 3(2): No person other than an institution may be granted a licence. An individual acting alone is neither a body of persons nor an undertaking.
#ASSERT `May I be granted a TVRO licence under regulation 3(2)?` (Date 1 6 2025) FALSE FALSE EQUALS "No."
#ASSERT `May I be granted a TVRO licence under regulation 3(2)?` (Date 1 6 2015) FALSE FALSE EQUALS "No."
#ASSERT `May I be granted a TVRO licence under regulation 3(2)?` (Date 1 6 2025) TRUE FALSE EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `May I be granted a TVRO licence under regulation 3(2)?` (Date 1 6 2025) FALSE TRUE EQUALS "Yes."
-- window of the Regulations as deposited: 29 February 2004 to 4 November 2026
#ASSERT `May I be granted a TVRO licence under regulation 3(2)?` (Date 29 2 2004) TRUE FALSE EQUALS "Yes."
-- S 354/2001 prints regulation 3(2) whole and is in operation from 1 August 2001, so the day before the Revised Edition is covered; before 1 August 2001 the text of regulation 3 was not obtained
#ASSERT `May I be granted a TVRO licence under regulation 3(2)?` (Date 28 2 2004) TRUE FALSE EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `May I be granted a TVRO licence under regulation 3(2)?` (Date 28 2 2004) FALSE FALSE EQUALS "No."
#ASSERT `May I be granted a TVRO licence under regulation 3(2)?` (Date 1 8 2001) FALSE FALSE EQUALS "No."
#ASSERT `May I be granted a TVRO licence under regulation 3(2)?` (Date 1 8 2001) TRUE FALSE EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `May I be granted a TVRO licence under regulation 3(2)?` (Date 31 7 2001) TRUE FALSE EQUALS "The Act, as deposited, does not say for that date."
#ASSERT `May I be granted a TVRO licence under regulation 3(2)?` (Date 1 10 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS "No."
#ASSERT `May I be granted a TVRO licence under regulation 3(2)?` (Date 5 11 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS "The Act, as deposited, does not say for that date."
#ASSERT `May I be granted a TVRO licence under regulation 3(2)?` (Date 1 1 2011) FALSE FALSE EQUALS "No."

§ `3A. Did the television and radio licensing regulations say I needed a licence?`

-- Argument order: kind; where it is; day of the conduct; day read as at; a ship station licence has been granted for the vessel; the use is temporary; the use is in a public place or at an official, social or charitable function.
-- Expected values are written from the Gazette text of regulations 23, 24, 27, 28 and 29 of the Revised Edition 2004 (BA1994-RG1.txt) and of S 333/2004 (BA1994-S333-2004.txt): reg 23(1) as printed names a vehicle or a vessel, reg 23(2) as amended names a vessel only;
-- reg 27(1) as printed prohibits operating a broadcast television receiver without a licence, and reg 27(1) as amended is an application provision; reg 28(2) a separate licence for a receiver installed in a vehicle or vessel; reg 29A (new, 21 June 2004) commercial properties;
-- S 548/2012 revokes the Regulations from 1 January 2011 (published 31 October 2012).

-- 1 March 2004, read on 1 March 2004: the Revised Edition as printed
#ASSERT `Did the Television and Radio Licensing Regulations say I needed a licence, for that conduct, with the law read as at that day?` "television" "at home or in other ordinary premises" (Date 1 3 2004) (Date 1 3 2004) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `Did the Television and Radio Licensing Regulations say I needed a licence, for that conduct, with the law read as at that day?` "television" "in a car or other road vehicle" (Date 1 3 2004) (Date 1 3 2004) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS "Yes."
